&lt;p data-start=&quot;4798&quot; data-end=&quot;4942&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;If you don’t meet 100% of the criteria, we still want to hear from you. Passion, curiosity, and impact orientation matter — tell us about yours.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Data Science  Lausanne, Vaud

Engagement Manager (Strategy & Data/AI Transformation) &lt;h2&gt;Who is Artefact?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is a next-generation strategy and data consulting firm dedicated to transforming organisations through data and AI. We combine the rigour of top-tier strategy consulting with deep expertise in data, digital and analytics to help clients achieve tangible business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With 2,500+ consultants, data scientists and engineers, we work with global leaders such as Samsung, L’Oréal, Orange and Sanofi. Our Zurich office is at the heart of Artefact’s growth, advising clients on their most pressing strategic challenges — from AI strategy and governance to digital transformation roadmaps and new business model design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Main Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engagement Manager in our Zurich or Lausanne office, you will work at the intersection of strategy consulting and data and AI delivery. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with client leadership teams to address high-stakes questions. How can AI reshape our business model? How should we govern and organise for data? Which strategic programmes deliver the most impact?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured Problem-Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Break complex challenges down into decisions a client can act on, combining consulting rigour with a working knowledge of what current AI can and cannot actually do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Design:&lt;/strong&gt; Turn a business question into a solution shape — what data it depends on, what kind of platform or product it should sit on, and what “good” looks like once it is built. You will do this alongside our data scientists and engineers, and you will be accountable for whether the design survives contact with production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Run engagements end to end, from hypothesis framing and market and competitor analysis through to data maturity assessments, client workshops, governance design and implementation roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feasibility &amp;amp; Economics:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the answer to &quot;will this work, and what will it cost&quot;. The evaluation approach, the unit economics per query or per case, and the point at which the business case stops closing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with C-level stakeholders and business unit leaders. You will build trusted relationships, communicate recommendations with clarity, and keep the work aligned to what the client is actually trying to decide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead mixed teams of consultants, data scientists and engineers. You are the person who can tell whether the technical plan is realistic, and the person the client believes when you say that it is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; Practice Building:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to the growth of Artefact&#39;s Zurich and Lausanne offices by shaping new offerings, creating intellectual capital - frameworks, thought pieces, benchmarks - and taking part in business development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Candidate Profile&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who can hold a technical position and a commercial one at the same time, and lead a team through both. The strongest candidates meet most of the following.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; A degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, Business, Economics or a related field. A strong technical foundation counts for more with us than where you studied.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Five to eight years across consulting and technology delivery, including at least one dedicated AI or data project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Acumen &amp;amp; AI Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; A strong dual affinity for business and technology. You have a deep working understanding of modern data and AI concepts — generative AI and LLMs, retrieval, predictive machine learning, cloud architectures — and of their practical business applications. You are capable of scoping AI use cases and of discussing technical constraints and opportunities confidently with C-level stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; You have owned the technical shape of AI work, not only its business case. You think in terms of enterprise architecture — how a solution fits the existing landscape, what it needs from data and governance, and how it scales from pilot to full rollout — and can defend those choices to technical and commercial stakeholders alike. You will not be writing production code, but you should have been close enough to it to be credible with the engineers with which you will collaborate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Problem-Solving Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong quantitative and analytical skills, and the judgement to know which number actually decides the question. You are comfortable getting to a defensible estimate with your assumptions stated out loud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Interpersonal Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent written and verbal communication. You can take a technical trade-off to a non-technical sponsor without flattening it, and be challenged by an engineer without retreating into abstraction. You enjoy working in teams and in front of clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluency in German/French and English, written and spoken, is strongly preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Eligibility:&lt;/strong&gt; You must be eligible to work in Switzerland.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy and the Build:&lt;/strong&gt; Artefact is neither a traditional strategy consultancy nor a pure technology player. You will move between the boardroom and the build, and be expected to be credible in both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineers, not hand-offs:&lt;/strong&gt; Our 2,500 people include the data scientists and engineers you will work beside on the same engagement - not a delivery organisation you hand a slide deck to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zurich Office Impact:&lt;/strong&gt; As part of a growing Swiss team you will have visibility and impact from the first day. You will help shape Artefact&#39;s footprint in the region and work directly with senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Regular training in both consulting method and AI and data capability, combined with international exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture of Doers:&lt;/strong&gt; Innovation, action, collaboration. We are entrepreneurial and fast-moving, committed to delivering impact while supporting each other&#39;s growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in &lt;strong&gt;Zürich or Lausanne&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Data Consulting  Lausanne, Vaud; Zürich

Senior Consultant - Business Analyst, Reporting & MIS (Private Banking) &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Joining Capco means joining an organization that is committed to an inclusive working environment where you’re encouraged to #BeYourselfAtWork. We celebrate individuality and recognize that diversity and inclusion, in all forms, is critical to success. It’s important to us that we recruit and develop as diverse a range of talent as we can and we believe that everyone brings something different to the table – so we’d love to know what makes you different. Such differences may mean we need to make changes to our process to allow you the best possible platform to succeed, and we are happy to cater to any reasonable adjustments you may require. You will find the section to let us know of these at the bottom of your application form or you can mention it directly to your recruiter at any stage and they will be happy to help.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Capco&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capco is a global technology and management consultancy dedicated to the financial services industry. We combine innovative thinking with unrivalled industry knowledge, to offer our clients consulting expertise, complex technology and package integration, transformation delivery and managed services to move their organizations forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We specialize primarily in banking &amp;amp; payments, capital markets, wealth &amp;amp; asset management, insurance and energy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have a collaborative and efficient approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We help our clients successfully innovate, increase revenue, manage risk and regulatory change, reduce costs and enhance controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We serve our clients from 32 offices across the Americas, Europe, and Asia Pacific&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If creativity and innovation are your passion, then Capco is right for you. You can grow in an inclusive, diverse and collaborative environment. At Capco, we will train and support you to help accelerate your career.&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW202573807 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior / Principal Consultant, you will play a key role in the functional design and further development of modern Management Reporting and Management Information Systems for Retail Banking, Corporate Banking, Private Banking, Wealth Management and Asset Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Acting as a Business Functional Analyst at the intersection of Business, Data, and IT, you will ensure that business requirements are translated into sustainable management reporting and steering solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will advise our clients on defining banking KPIs, enhancing reporting processes, and modernizing existing MIS landscapes. In addition to contributing your functional expertise, you will actively support client development, project management, and the continued development of our Banking Consulting capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR CAPCO DAY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise local and international banks on the development and enhancement of Management Information Systems and reporting landscapes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take functional ownership as a Business Functional Analyst, working across Business, Data, and IT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, harmonize, and further develop banking KPIs for Retail Banking, Corporate Banking, Private Banking, Wealth Management and Asset Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex business requirements into functional concepts, reporting logic, and functional requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and optimize reporting processes and data journeys across the entire reporting value chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and facilitate workshops with business divisions/functions and senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support testing, KPI validation, and the implementation of new reporting solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR CAPCO FIT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5–6 years of experience in consulting or in a business function within a private bank&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in Reporting and Management Information Systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth understanding of products and processes within Retail Banking, Corporate Banking, Private Banking, Wealth Management and/or Asset Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a Business Analyst or Functional Analyst in regulatory or business transformation projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very good knowledge of banking KPIs, management reporting, and sales steering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Business, Data, and IT stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience facilitating workshops and managing stakeholders at management level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and structured approach, combined with well-developed consulting skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in German and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NICE TO HAVE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience transforming global reporting and MIS landscapes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience migrating MIS and reporting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of cloud data platforms and modern BI architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing stakeholders at senior/executive management level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHY CAPCO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A career at Capco is a chance to help reshape the competitive landscape in financial services. We launch new banks, transform existing ones, and help our clients navigate complex change. As consultants, we work on the front-end business design all the way through to technology implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are the largest Financial Services focused consultancy in the world, serving everyone from global banks to emerging FinTechs, from strategy through digital transformation, design, business consulting, data and analytics, cyber, cloud, technology architecture, and engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capco is a young and growing firm. We maintain an entrepreneurial spirit and growth mindset, and have minimal bureaucracy. We have no internal silos that get in the way of your career opportunities or ability to focus on our clients and make a difference to the business. We offer the opportunity for everyone to learn rapidly, take on tough challenges, and get promoted quickly. We take pride in our creative, collaborative, diverse, and inclusive culture, where everyone can #BYAW.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer highly competitive benefits, flexible working hours, technical and soft skills training, smartphone &amp;amp; fast mobile internet and a work culture focused on innovation and creation of lasting value for our clients and employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ready to take the Next Step&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds like you, we would love to hear from you. &amp;nbsp;This is an opportunity to make a difference and contribute to a highly successful company with a significant growth trajectory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Business Consulting

Staff Security Engineer, Incident Response &lt;p&gt;RDQ327R180&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff Security Engineer, Incident Response&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Incident Response team&#39;s mission is to respond to security threats, incidents and investigations to protect our customers, employees and enterprise data in a fast, efficient and standardised manner. We&#39;re a tight-knit team of security incident responders and incident handlers doing &quot;Security for Databricks on Databricks&quot;, using our own platform to create near-real-time log analytics, alerting and forensics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be an individual contributor on the security Incident Response (IR) team at Databricks, reporting to the regional IR manager. You will be responsible for conducting security analysis and forensics, responding to high-priority alerts and contributing to automations and agentic capabilities. You will be a security multiplier and help the team scale security incident response at Databricks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will respond to incidents as part of a distributed 24x7 operations and on-call schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will triage and respond to security events and alerts, ensuring quick and effective containment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will conduct analysis and forensics across a range of data sources to determine the timeline and impact of security events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will provide technical leadership and influence team direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will develop solutions, including leveraging AI and agentic platforms, to deliver autonomous capabilities, expedite your work and scale the impact of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will communicate technical decisions through design docs and tech talks, and mentor junior security responders via security guidance, design reviews and code reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree AND 7+ years experience in Incident Response work OR Master&#39;s Degree AND 5+ years experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud security expertise in at least 1 of AWS, GCP or Azure, and proficiency in the others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in AI/LLM and agentic capabilities. Prefer experience with building and operating agentic systems in a security setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad security subject matter expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in a few core IR skills (DFIR , Reverse Engineering, Traditional Network Security, Storage and access security, Sandboxing, Compute security, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Enterprise Security and SaaS applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of a SIEM and SOAR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building Incident Response Tooling, scripting language skills and experience with AI coding tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
